<h2 id="borrowing">Borrowing</h2>
<ul>
  <li>A slice such as <code>s[1..3]</code> or <code>xs.span</code> borrows from its owner. It owns nothing.</li>
  <li>While a borrow is still used, changing the owner is BYN3004.</li>
  <li><code>copy()</code> turns a borrowed slice into an owned value.</li>
</ul>
<example name="ref-memory-borrow"/>
<pre><code class="byn">var xs: List&lt;i64&gt; = [1, 2, 3]
let s = xs.span
xs.append(4)
print($"{s.length}")</code></pre>
<figure class="diag">
<pre><span class="err">error BYN3004:</span> `xs` is modified while `s` still borrows it
  --&gt; mm-borrow.byn:3:1

<span class="gut">  3 │</span> xs.append(4)
<span class="gut">    │</span> <span class="hl">^^^^^^^^^^^^ `s` is used again on line 4</span>
<span class="gut">    │</span>
  help: finish using `s` first, or copy what it needs before changing `xs`</pre>
  <figcaption>The compiler’s message for this program.</figcaption>
</figure>

